{"kind":"request","text":"R14 child: a Worker-wide scope census (registered scopes and their genesis pins), from your 0321a0f8.\n\nWhat: an authorized, bounded listing of the scope index so that an operator can enumerate every registered scope on a Worker and, through the existing `scope-index versions --manifest`, each one's definition pin. This is the one observation R14 still needs (ruling 7d5cbfcf, point 2) and it is also the Worker-wide installed-release inventory that the R11 deploy rule lacked (the operator listing covered only the operator's own repository, checker 578b5da4).\n\nDesign (decided):\n1. ScopeIndexPort and the deployed ScopeIndex gain `list(after, limit)` over the existing ScopeIndexRows.list, limit at most 100, cursor the last row's scope, served only to an operator session (the same authorization as the listing's operator session path, 6499a12b), never to a member or anonymous caller, and only in enforce mode; register mode answers `unsupported`.\n2. The CLI gains `dap scope-index census --out FILE`: pages the listing to completion under one bounded budget (at most 100 pages), writes a v1 manifest in the existing {at, genesis} row form with the Worker's service and root, and records `absent`, `unsupported` and `empty` as distinct outcomes, plus any failed page with its cursor so that a partial census is never read as complete. Concurrent registration during pagination is qualified in the output (rows registered after the first page may be missing), never silently.\n3. `scope-index versions --manifest` runs over that file unchanged, and its report is the pin census: for each row, the definition pin or an explicit unavailable, mismatch or unsupported outcome.\n4. No new pin column, no newest-pin substitution, no change to has/register, no census of unregistered legacy objects (they stay a stated gap).\n\nWitness: on the test Worker, a census of a fleet with n registered scopes lists n rows and `versions` reports every pin; a census under register mode answers unsupported; a member session is refused; a page failure leaves the output marked incomplete; a paired control shows the operator listing of 6499a12b still reading only the operator's repository. Ordinary gate, exact-head review, PD-2 note and manifest. The head's note lists the deploy step; the planner deploys all three Workers and files the first census of each.\n\nOrder: after the archive settlement head and the R14 documents head; before the standing release items.","body":{"conditions":"listing served only to an operator session in enforce mode; census output distinguishes absent, unsupported, empty and incomplete; versions report over the census gives each pin or an explicit outcome; member session refused; ordinary gate; exact-head review; PD-2 note and manifest; planner deploys and files the first census per Worker","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}